The young people want a skatepark with proper ramps. {{1}}
Playing football and sitting quietly cannot happen on the same patch of playground at the same time – the wishes clash. {{2}}
The class agrees: music is allowed during the main break, but only through headphones. {{3}}
By collecting 300 signatures, the young people get the local council to listen to them. {{4}}
The resident wants one thing above all: peace and quiet in the evening. {{5}}
The local council has the final say and can put the decision into effect. {{6}}
Yes to a skatepark – but on the outskirts and with quiet hours from 20:00: both sides give a little. {{7}}
Two groups want to use the same sports hall on Wednesday afternoon – they cannot both have it at once. {{8}}
